alert.description:
`depleted` when the balance is gone and work is spilling over;
`expiring` when a balance remains but the block expires in-window;
`none` when healthy.

CreditNoteApplication.description:
One allocation of credit-note value onto an invoice. The money move
itself is the paired invoice payment receipt (provider `credit_note`);
this row is the credit-side ledger.

DispositionStatus.description:
The human verification disposition of one time entry (Wave 39 V1).
`rejected` and `non_billable` demand the typed [`UnbillableReason`];
the workspace badge set matches this vocabulary exactly.

ManifestClientWorkflowOverride.description:
One per-client workflow override row, verbatim. `state` is
`set` (value overrides the org default) or `disabled` (explicit deny);
an absent row means the client inherits and exports nothing.

never.description:
true = "never show this again" (persists the dismissed flag);
false = plain "skip for now" (a no-op that intentionally records
nothing — the step stays pending and resumable).

model.description:
Embedding model identifier. Required when `embedding` is supplied;
defaults to the org's configured embedding model when Core embeds a
`text` chunk.

status.description:
`"proposal"` = a rewrite is offered for the user's Apply/Discard;
`"unavailable"` = the provider seam is not configured — Tier-1
Tidy remains fully functional.

SecretFieldValuePatch.description:
PATCH field entry (A5, Wave 16 lane 9): `value: null` CLEARS the
sealed field (row deleted, audited via the record-updated event);
a value rotates the sealed ciphertext.

TicketsByCategory.description:
Tickets by workflow category. The status NAME is per-board and repeats
across boards, so a name-keyed map would merge different statuses;
`category` is the closed vocabulary the workflow layer owns.

delete.summary:
DELETE /api/boards/{id}/members/{user_id} — removes one membership;
the user falls back to org-governed access. Emits
`board.membership_removed`.

post.summary:
POST /api/config-items/merge-candidates/{id}/defer — park the candidate
out of the pending queue WITHOUT deciding it (reversible via restore;
a feed upsert refreshes evidence but never un-defers silently).

patch.summary:
PATCH /api/kb/articles/{id} — instant-first (IF1/IF2). Archived
articles refuse title/body edits until unarchived (typed conflict);
status flips stay legal.

post.summary:
POST /api/onboarding/reset/org — admin re-run of the org wizard: clears
every per-step flag (the flows_disabled switch is untouched on purpose;
re-running a disabled family stays silent until re-enabled).

get.summary:
GET /api/v1/reply-snippets/{id} — fetch one snippet (cross-lane fix,
Wave 34 lane 4: the fork-on-edit flow reads the origin after forking;
the route was missing so reads 405'd).

GET /api/tickets/{id}/presence — current viewers/editors of the
ticket, TTL-pruned. The ticket must exist in the caller's org (RLS);
the roster is org-keyed, so it can never leak across orgs.
